# Backend rules

- Use NestJS with Fastify adapter.
- Keep the application a modular monolith.
- Controllers are thin: validate/authorize/translate transport concerns and call application services.
- Business logic belongs in services/use-cases/domain packages, not controllers or Prisma models.
- External systems must be behind adapters: payments, AI providers, object storage, email, etc.
- Dependency direction should point inward toward domain/application abstractions.
- Validate all HTTP input and all external responses before trusting them.
- Authentication and authorization are distinct. Always verify resource ownership for user-scoped resources.
- Use centralized error mapping. Do not leak provider/internal stack details to clients.
- Propagate a request/correlation ID into logs, AI request records and background jobs.
- Prefer explicit DTO/contracts from `packages/contracts` for web/API boundaries.
- Never perform authoritative financial calculations in controllers.
- Never perform long-running video/agent jobs synchronously in a request lifecycle.

Future logical modules include `Auth`, `Users`, `Plans`, `Subscriptions`, `Payments`, `Usage`, `Ai`, `Chats`, `Files`, `Generations`, `Agents`, `Admin`. Create modules only when their phase requires them.
